Yes. PaRC v2 resolves the main v1 objections enough for a single-domain pilot.

The λ-mixture makes the pony floor valid as a validation-gated deployment rule, with one caveat: it is not a mathematical test-set floor because λ can overfit validation. That is acceptable if you report test degradation risk and kill when λ is unstable or near zero.

The revised gate is much better. Requiring NDCG lift first, then treating cyclic/intransitive structure as a separate scientific finding, fixes the earlier criterion error. The novelty claim is now scoped: comparative residual over a specific frozen pointwise posterior, not universal absence from pointwise scorers.

No remaining fatal flaw before pilot compute. The main risks are nonfatal but must be pre-registered: pilot-domain selection must not be outcome-picked after seeing PaRC; cache reuse may be limited because prompts are user-history-specific; and compute-normalized value must be reported even if raw lift clears +0.005.

Proceed to ARIS experiment-plan for one domain only, not 8-domain scale-out.

NOVELTY: 8/10
FEASIBILITY: 7/10
